            "Steps 3a and 3b start at the same time in different lanes, so they are drawn side by side. The laptop branch takes 5 days; the accounts-plus-approval branch takes about 3.5 days. The longer branch sets the duration, exactly as the [critical path](/project-management/critical-path-method/) does in a project schedule. The diagram therefore gives HR a simple rule: trigger the request at least six working days before the start date, or the new starter arrives without a laptop.",
            "It also shows why a system can deserve its own lane. Step 3b involves no person, but if the HR record is incomplete it fails silently. Giving the system a lane prompts the question: who is told when this step fails?",
