            "Ask three questions of every step: does it add value for the customer of the process, does it need to be done by this lane, and does it need to happen in this order? Steps that fail all three are candidates for removal.",
            "If you need to find the root cause of a recurring problem, such as frequent rework at one step, a [fishbone diagram](/project-management/fishbone-diagram/) is a good next tool. For broader waste reduction, swimlane analysis fits naturally with [Lean project management](/project-management/lean-project-management/) and [Six Sigma](/project-management/six-sigma/) methods.",
