            "The word 'swimlane' also appears in two other planning tools. On a Kanban board, swimlanes are horizontal rows that separate types of work, teams or priority levels on the same board; see [Kanban swimlanes](/project-management/kanban/kanban-swimlanes/). On a Gantt chart, swimlanes group tasks by team or workstream so you can see parallel work at a glance. Both borrow the same idea of lanes, but neither is a process map.",
            "See our [guide to the RACI matrix](/project-management/raci-matrix/) to turn the lanes on your diagram into clear accountability.",
